  "id": "primary-process",
  "term": "primary process",
  "definition": "In this historical medical-psychological usage, a primary process is the change or lesion thought to be the original disease process from which other tissue changes and symptoms develop. The passage uses the term for the suspected first pathological change, while noting uncertainty about which bodily system is affected first.",
